{
  "assessment": "The source provides two temperature branches (T=10^-6 and T=1) for the incompressible kinetic energy E_i versus quench duration tau_Q, with fitted power laws and statistical details. The reviewer figure evidence confirms the fitted curves cover tau_Q from 100 to 1000 for both branches. This supports a quantitative interactive experiment with tau_Q as a numeric control and E_i as a numeric readout, with two branch-specific fixed conditions. The case is authoring-ready.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Seong-Ho Shinn, Spontaneous Quantum Turbulence in a Newborn Bose-Einstein Condensate via the Kibble-Zurek Mechanism, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/b16v-hwp2",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/b16v-hwp2",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2506.21670v3"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper establishes spontaneous quantum turbulence (SQT) in a newborn 2D Bose-Einstein condensate via the Kibble-Zurek mechanism, focusing on the incompressible kinetic energy spectrum and its universal scaling with quench duration. The selected cluster is the incompressible kinetic energy E_i at equilibration time as a function of quench duration tau_Q for two temperature branches (T=10^-6 and T=1).",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "KZ_Ei_scaling",
      "statement": "The incompressible kinetic energy E_i at equilibration time scales with quench duration as E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-(1+2 nu)/(1+z nu)}, with mean-field exponents nu=1/2 and z=2 giving E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-1}.",
      "equations": [
        "E_i \\propto \\tau_Q^{-(1+2\\nu)/(1+z\\nu)}",
        "E_i = (19.774 \\pm 5.010) \\times 10^4 \\, \\tau_Q^{-0.971 \\pm 0.052} (T=10^{-6})",
        "E_i = (9.543 \\pm 2.951) \\times 10^4 \\, \\tau_Q^{-0.935 \\pm 0.068} (T=1)"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["E_i", "tau_Q", "nu", "z"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "Ei_amplitude_T_low",
          "value": 197740.0,
          "uncertainty": "\\pm 5.010 \\times 10^4 (source_unspecified)",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "Amplitude of the fitted power law for E_i at T=10^-6",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 443,
              "line_end": 443,
              "support": "Fitted power law E_i = (19.774 ± 5.010) × 10^4 tau_Q^{-0.971 ± 0.052} for panel (a) at T=10^-6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Ei_exponent_T_low",
